# ChatComposer

<script setup lang="ts">
import { ref } from 'vue'

const text = ref('')
const sent = ref<string[]>([])

function onSend(payload: { text: string }) {
  sent.value.unshift(payload.text)
  text.value = ''
}
</script>

## Basic Usage

### ChatComposer
:::TuffDemoWrapper{demo="ChatComposerChatComposerDemo" code-lang="vue"}
---
code: |
  <template>
    <TxChatComposer v-model="text" @send="onSend" />
  </template>
---
:::

### Tray Placement

The `tray` slot hangs a flat tray outside the card. `trayPlacement` puts it below the card (the default) or above it. When the placement changes:

1. The outgoing tray content fades out with a slight blur.
2. About 70ms later, the card slides across by one tray row.
3. The incoming content is already in place. It is uncovered as the card moves away, not faded in.

When both trays are the same height, the composer's outer box does not change size.

:::TuffDemoWrapper{demo="ChatComposerTrayDemo" code-lang="vue"}
---
code: |
  <template>
    <TxChatComposer v-model="text" :tray-placement="placement" tray-label="Context" show-attachment-button>
      <template #tray>
        <TxModeChip v-if="placement === 'bottom'" icon="i-carbon-plug" label="Connect apps" @click="placement = 'top'" />
        <TxModeChip v-else icon="i-carbon-folder" label="Select a project" @click="placement = 'bottom'" />
      </template>
    </TxChatComposer>
  </template>
---
:::

### With a Mode Chip

Put a [ModeChip](/docs/dev/components/mode-chip) in `toolbar-left`. When the mode changes, the chip morphs in place: the icon swaps with a scale, the label crossfades through a blur, the tint fades in, and the width follows the new label.

:::TuffDemoWrapper{demo="ChatComposerModeChipDemo" code-lang="vue"}
---
code: |
  <template>
    <TxChatComposer v-model="text">
      <template #toolbar-left>
        <TxModeChip
          :icon="unrestricted ? 'i-carbon-unlocked' : 'i-carbon-touch-1'"
          :label="unrestricted ? 'Unrestricted access' : 'Request approval'"
          :tone="unrestricted ? 'danger' : 'muted'"
          @click="unrestricted = !unrestricted"
        />
      </template>
    </TxChatComposer>
  </template>
---
:::

## API

### Props

| Name | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `modelValue` | `string` | `''` | Textarea `v-model` value |
| `placeholder` | `string` | `'Message…'` | Textarea placeholder |
| `ariaLabel` | `string` | - | Accessible name for the textarea; falls back to `placeholder` |
| `disabled` | `boolean` | `false` | Disables input, send, and attachment actions |
| `submitting` | `boolean` | `false` | Blocks sending while a request is in flight |
| `allowAttachmentWhileSubmitting` | `boolean` | `false` | Allows attachment actions during submit |
| `minRows` | `number` | `3` | Resting textarea height in rows; the textarea grows past it as the text grows |
| `maxRows` | `number` | `6` | Row cap for that growth; the textarea scrolls beyond it. Never lower than `minRows` |
| `sendOnEnter` | `boolean` | `true` | Enables keyboard send behavior |
| `sendOnMetaEnter` | `boolean` | `true` | Requires Meta/Ctrl+Enter for keyboard send |
| `allowEmptySend` | `boolean` | `false` | Allows attachment-only sends when text is empty |
| `sendButtonText` | `string` | `'Send'` | Accessible name of the send icon button |
| `showAttachmentButton` | `boolean` | `false` | Shows the default `+` attachment button |
| `attachmentButtonText` | `string` | `'Attach'` | Accessible name of the `+` attachment button |
| `attachments` | `ChatComposerAttachment[]` | `[]` | Attachment chips rendered above the textarea |
| `trayPlacement` | `'top' \| 'bottom'` | `'bottom'` | Puts the tray above or below the card; changing it runs the placement motion |
| `trayLabel` | `string` | - | When set, the tray renders as a `role="group"` with this name |

### Events

| Name | Payload | Description |
|------|---------|-------------|
| `update:modelValue` | `string` | Emitted on textarea input |
| `send` | `{ text: string }` | Emitted with trimmed text when sending is allowed |
| `attachmentClick` | - | Emitted when attachment action is allowed |
| `paste` | `ClipboardEvent` | Forwarded textarea paste event |
| `attachmentAdd` | `File[]` | Files pasted or dropped in; the host owns the upload |
| `focus` | `FocusEvent` | Forwarded textarea focus event |
| `blur` | `FocusEvent` | Forwarded textarea blur event |

### Slots

| Name | Scope | Description |
|------|-------|-------------|
| `tray` | - | Context tray content outside the card; `trayPlacement` sets its side |
| `attachments` | `{ attachments }` | Replace default attachment chips |
| `toolbar` | `{ send, disabled, attachmentClick }` | Replace the default action row |
| `toolbar-left` | `{ disabled }` | Add content to the left side of the default action row |
| `actions` | `{ send, disabled }` | Add content before the default send button |
| `footer` | - | Render inside the card, below the action row |

### CSS Variables

| Variable | Default | Description |
|----------|---------|-------------|
| `--tx-chat-composer-radius` | `18px` | Corner radius shared by the shell and the card |

## Interaction Contract

- `send` trims text before emitting the payload.
- Empty text blocks sending unless `allowEmptySend=true` and attachments exist.
- `disabled` and `submitting` block sending; `disabled` also blocks attachment actions.
- Attachment actions are blocked while submitting unless `allowAttachmentWhileSubmitting=true`.
- With `sendOnMetaEnter=true`, keyboard send requires Meta/Ctrl+Enter; with it off, Enter sends and Shift+Enter keeps a newline.
- A custom `toolbar` receives callable `send` / `attachmentClick` functions and replaces the default action row.
- The textarea grows with its content from `minRows` lines and scrolls once it reaches `maxRows` (`field-sizing: content`). Browsers without that feature keep a fixed `minRows` and scroll.
- The root is the shell. Fallthrough classes and attributes land on the shell; the white input surface is `.tx-chat-composer__card`. The DOM is the same with or without a tray, so adding a tray never recreates the textarea, and focus and IME state survive.
- The tray renders only when the `tray` slot is provided. The placement timeline:
  - the outgoing tray leaves the flow, pinned to its own side, and fades out over 200ms with a 2px blur;
  - 70ms in, the card slides across over 450ms on `cubic-bezier(0.65, 0.16, 0.1, 0.88)`, with no overshoot;
  - the incoming tray has no entrance; the card uncovers it.
- When a tray appears or disappears, or the two trays differ in height, the shell height animates on the same timeline.
- If focus was inside the leaving tray, it moves to the textarea after the swap instead of being stranded on a node that is going away.
- Under `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`, or where the Web Animations API is missing, the swap lands on the final layout at once.
- The attachment and send controls are native `<button>`s. The `+` changes only its ink on hover, instantly, with no plate; the send button keeps its solid fill and does not change on hover. The only transition on either is the press scale.

## Best Practices

- Keep `modelValue` controlled in the host and clear it only after the send handler accepts the payload.
- Treat `send` as an intent event, not a delivery guarantee; failed API calls should keep enough host state to retry.
- Use `submitting` to prevent duplicate sends while a request is in flight.
- Prefer Meta/Ctrl+Enter for dense chat inputs where Enter should remain available for line breaks.
- Use `attachments` for status chips only; upload progress, removal, and retry behavior should stay in the host or a custom `attachments` slot.
- Keep tray content to one line, and keep the top and bottom trays the same height, so a swap does not resize the outer box.
- Use a muted `TxModeChip`, or a button with the same ink-only hover, for tray actions. Do not add a plate.
- Let context drive the tray's side ("Connect apps" becoming "Select a project"). Do not loop the swap as decoration.
- Hosts that styled `.tx-chat-composer` as the card should retarget those rules to `.tx-chat-composer__card`.

## Review Notes

- Source: `packages/tuffex/packages/components/src/chat/src/TxChatComposer.vue` confirms:
  - controlled textarea updates, trimmed send payloads, the attachment-only guard and attachment-button gating;
  - keyboard send modes, scoped toolbar functions and forwarded native textarea events;
  - the shell/card structure and the tray placement choreography.
- Motion reference: [@flohoeller's Chatbox component clip](https://x.com/flohoeller/status/2102660458658582913). The slide curve is a least-squares fit to the clip's frame-by-frame samples, 0.87 video px off; standard curves are 2px or more off.
- Rejected designs:
  - fading the incoming tray in, because the reference uncovers it rather than fading it;
  - the clip's 120ms hover ease, because it breaks the "hover colour changes are immediate" design rule;
  - making the shell the root only while a tray exists, because that recreated the textarea and dropped focus and IME state.
- In the dark theme `--tx-fill-color-blank` is transparent, so the card paints `--tx-bg-color` underneath; otherwise the tray would show through while the card slides.
- Tray text uses `--tx-text-color-regular`: secondary ink on the tray fill measures 2.87:1 in the light theme.
- Type contracts: `packages/tuffex/packages/components/src/chat/src/types.ts` defines `ChatComposerProps`, `ChatComposerTrayPlacement`, `ChatComposerAttachment`, and `ChatComposerEmits`. The component declares its props as a runtime object so the dev servers see new fields.
- **Verified coverage:** Coverage:
  - `chat/__tests__/chat-composer.test.ts` covers default rendering, model updates, trimmed sends, keyboard modes, blocked sends, attachment-only sends, attachment guards, scoped slots, native events, and install registration;
  - `chat-composer-tray.test.ts` covers tray placement and labelling, the runtime props, textarea reuse, the slide and resize, interruption, focus handoff, reduced motion, no-WAAPI, and SSR;
  - `chat-composer-style.test.ts` pins the compiled style: no colour transitions, no hover plate, the out-of-flow leaving tray, no entrance styles for the incoming tray, reduced motion, ring plus one elevation step, an opaque card, and an inherited font.
- Export: `packages/tuffex/packages/components/src/chat/index.ts` exports `ChatComposer`, `TxChatComposer`, and public composer types.

